What will you do?

Do you have an affinity for technology or experience in technical production, and are you handy with practical work? Are you also looking for a long-term job opportunity? Then look no further!

As a Field Service Technician, you will visit various organizations, ranging from large government institutions and universities to hospitals. The work requires specialized skills, for which you will receive internal training.

Your responsibilities include:

- Maintenance and renovation of air handling systems;
- Cleaning and gas-free preparation of installations within the chemical industry;
- Collaborating with various clients to ensure technical installations function optimally.

Who are you?

In addition to an interest in technology and technical insight, you have:

- A VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- A valid Category B driving license;
- Strong communication skills, customer friendliness, and initiative;
- Good command of the English and/or Dutch language.

Are you a real hands-on person who enjoys staying physically active? We are looking for a Warehouse Employee to join the team of a family-owned company in the meat industry. You will work in a refrigerated environment and mainly be responsible for picking and moving meat products.

It is important that you are comfortable working in cold temperatures. To keep you properly protected, you will be provided with a warm jacket, trousers and gloves.

What will you do?

As a Warehouse Employee, you and your colleagues will make sure that orders are prepared correctly and on time. You will work with various meat products and stay physically active throughout your shift.

Your responsibilities will include:

- Picking meat products based on customer orders;
- Picking and preparing orders for shipment;
- Moving crates containing meat products;
- Lifting crates weighing up to approximately 20 kg;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Keeping the warehouse clean, tidy and organized;
- Supporting colleagues with various warehouse activities;
- Handling products carefully and following applicable hygiene regulations.

You will be working in a refrigerated environment, so you must be comfortable working in the cold throughout your shift. To help you work comfortably and safely, you will receive protective clothing, including a warm jacket, trousers and gloves.

Working days and hours

Monday: 06:00/07:00 – 12:00/14:00Thursday: 06:00/07:00 – 12:00/14:00Sunday: 06:00/07:00 – 12:00/14:00

- You are a real hands-on person and enjoy physical work;
- You are physically fit and able to lift and move crates weighing up to 20 kg;
- You have no problem working with meat products;
- You are comfortable working in a refrigerated environment;
- You are able to work independently and take responsibility for your tasks;
- You are reliable and keep your commitments;
- You speak Dutch and/or English;

As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse operation. Together with your colleagues, you make sure orders are processed efficiently and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Operating an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Loading and unloading goods;
- Checking products for accuracy and completeness;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workplace.

Thanks to a structured onboarding program, you'll quickly learn all aspects of the job.

- Are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Have a basic understanding of Dutch and/or English;
- Enjoy physical and active work;
- Work accurately and responsibly;
- Are motivated and eager to learn.

Previous logistics experience is a plus, but not required.

SamenvattingStart as an Orderpicker in Woerden and help keep Jumbo stores stocked across the Netherlands. Earn up to €23.39 gross per hour, and enjoy a hands-on logistics job with clear routines and a supportive team. No specific education required, just motivation and a willingness to learn. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker, you’ll prepare orders for Jumbo stores across the Netherlands using a modern voice-pick system. Depending on the assignment, you will work in a warm (+18°C) or chilled (+2°C to +4°C) area at the warehouse.

Your tasks:
-  Picking orders with a voice-pick system;
-  Placing products on trolleys or pallets;
-  Checking orders for accuracy and quality;
-  Keeping your workspace clean and organized;
-  Following warehouse and safety procedures;

This job is for 32–40 hours per week in a two-shift system, with occasional weekend work.
The worktimes are from 06.00 - 14:00 and 14.00 - 21:00.
Over het bedrijfAt Jumbo’s distribution centre in Woerden, teamwork keeps things moving. Every day, colleagues work together to prepare orders and make sure stores across the Netherlands receive the groceries and everyday products their customers need. You will join a modern, well-organized workplace where everyone plays a part. Clear procedures, a focus on quality and helpful colleagues make it a great place to gain experience in logistics and develop your skills.
Wat wij vragen- Own accommodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- Basic English skills to understand instructions and communicate with your team
- Willingness to work in warm and chilled areas;
- Physically stable and comfortable with walking and lifting during the shift;
- You are available to work in 2-shifts.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.
Wat wij bieden- A salary between €14.99 and €15.21 gross per hour for work in the warm warehouse and €15.37–€15.59

